  "body": "Load the following HTML:\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<form action=\"http://www.google.com/\">\n  <input name=q value=\"html\">\n</form>\n<script>\nvar form = document.forms[0];\nform.parentNode.removeChild(form);\nform.submit();\n</script>\n<p>Submitted?</p>\n```\n- Edge and Firefox: The form is not submitted silently.\n- WebKit and Blink: The form is submitted, and the page is navigated.\n\nAccording to the current specification, the algorithm has no step to reject form submission in an orphan DOM tree.  So the WebKit/Blink behavior conforms to the specification.  However, navigating to another URL by an orphan form looks weird to me. \n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/forms.html#form-submission-algorithm\n",
